<title>POLAND: Zloty fixed weaker at 0.36 pct from parity rate.</title>
<headline>Zloty fixed weaker at 0.36 pct from parity rate.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland fixed the zloty at 3.2325 to the dollar, down from 3.2095 on Monday and at 1.8970 to the mark, up from 1.8995, the NBP said.</p>
<p>The central bank fixed the zloty at an average of 0.36 percent from the weighted dollar and mark parity rates, weaker than Monday's 0.62 percent fix.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
